{"path":"cargo/reference/pkgid-spec.html","title":"Package ID Specifications","description":"Subcommands of Cargo frequently need to refer to a particular package within a dependency graph for various operations like updating, cleaning, building, etc. To solve this problem, Cargo supports…","body":{"type":"document","children":[{"type":"heading","level":1,"id":"package-id-specifications","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package ID Specifications"}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"id":"package-id-specifications-1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package ID specifications"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Subcommands of Cargo frequently need to refer to a particular package within a dependency graph for various operations like updating, cleaning, building, etc. To solve this problem, Cargo supports "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package ID Specifications"}]},{"type":"text","value":". A specification is a string which is used to uniquely refer to one package within a graph of packages."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The specification may be fully qualified, such as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#regex@1.4.3"},{"type":"text","value":" or it may be abbreviated, such as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"},{"type":"text","value":". The abbreviated form may be used as long as it uniquely identifies a single package in the dependency graph. If there is ambiguity, additional qualifiers can be added to make it unique. For example, if there are two versions of the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"},{"type":"text","value":" package in the graph, then it can be qualified with a version to make it unique, such as "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex@1.4.3"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Package ID specifications output by cargo, for example in "},{"type":"link","href":"https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/commands/cargo-metadata.html","title":null,"children":[{"type":"text","value":"cargo metadata"}]},{"type":"text","value":" output, are fully qualified."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"specification-grammar","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Specification grammar"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The formal grammar for a Package Id Specification is:"}]},{"type":"code_block","language":"notrust","code":"spec := pkgname |\n        [ kind \"+\" ] proto \"://\" hostname-and-path [ \"?\" query] [ \"#\" ( pkgname | semver ) ]\nquery = ( \"branch\" | \"tag\" | \"rev\" ) \"=\" ref\npkgname := name [ (\"@\" | \":\" ) semver ]\nsemver := digits [ \".\" digits [ \".\" digits [ \"-\" prerelease ] [ \"+\" build ]]]\n\nkind = \"registry\" | \"git\" | \"path\"\nproto := \"http\" | \"git\" | \"file\" | ..."},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Here, brackets indicate that the contents are optional."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The URL form can be used for git dependencies, or to differentiate packages that come from different sources such as different registries."}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"example-specifications","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example specifications"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following are references to the "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"},{"type":"text","value":" package on "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"crates.io"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec"}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Name"}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version"}]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"*"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex@1.4"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.4.*"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex@1.4.3"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.4.3"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"*"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#regex@1.4.3"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.4.3"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index#regex@1.4.3"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.4.3"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The following are some examples of specs for several different git dependencies:"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec"}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Name"}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version"}]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo#0.52.0"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"0.52.0"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"https://github.com/rust-lang/cargo#cargo-platform@0.1.2"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"cargo-platform"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"0.1.2"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"ssh://git@github.com/rust-lang/regex.git#regex@1.4.3"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.4.3"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"git+ssh://git@github.com/rust-lang/regex.git#regex@1.4.3"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.4.3"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"git+ssh://git@github.com/rust-lang/regex.git?branch=dev#regex@1.4.3"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"regex"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.4.3"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Local packages on the filesystem can use "},{"type":"inline_code","code":"file://"},{"type":"text","value":" URLs to reference them:"}]},{"type":"table","headers":[{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec"}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Name"}]},{"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Version"}]}],"rows":[{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"file:///path/to/my/project/foo"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"foo"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"*"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"file:///path/to/my/project/foo#1.1.8"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"foo"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.1.8"}]}]},{"cells":[{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"path+file:///path/to/my/project/foo#1.1.8"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"foo"}]},{"children":[{"type":"inline_code","code":"1.1.8"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"id":"brevity-of-specifications","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Brevity of specifications"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The goal of this is to enable both succinct and exhaustive syntaxes for referring to packages in a dependency graph. Ambiguous references may refer to one or more packages. Most commands generate an error if more than one package could be referred to with the same specification."}]}]}}
